Silo patch 0002 — cfgmgr32: inert CM_NOTIFY_FILTER_TYPE_DEVICEINSTANCE notifications

Symptom: TEKKEN 8 (and other Steam games) crash on EVERY exit — Unreal's "Fatal error!" dialog, a new
Saved/Crashes/UECC-* directory each time. Diagnosed 2026-09-26: the crash is in SteamAPI_Shutdown →
steamclient64 → CM_Unregister_Notification → sechost!I_ScUnregisterDeviceNotification, with a handle that
points into steamclient64's .rdata. The same crash happens in CrossOver 26.3's own bottle (29 of 34 crash
reports), so it is upstream behaviour, not Silo's.

Cause: create_notify_context() returns CR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED for CM_NOTIFY_FILTER_TYPE_DEVICEINSTANCE
WITHOUT writing *notify_handle, and steamclient64 doesn't check the return value: it later unregisters
whatever garbage was in its variable.

Fix (minimal, two lines of behaviour):
  * CM_Register_Notification() sets *notify_context = NULL up front, so no failure path leaves it
    uninitialised (unregistering NULL returns CR_INVALID_DATA cleanly);
  * DEVICEINSTANCE returns CR_SUCCESS with a context that has no registration (ctx->notify == NULL): it never
    fires, and CM_Unregister_Notification frees it safely — I_ScUnregisterDeviceNotification(NULL) returns
    FALSE immediately. Windows supports this filter type, so "succeeds, delivers no events" is closer to
    Windows than an error nobody checks.

Verify: clean exit from TEKKEN 8 on a runtime built with this patch — no new Saved/Crashes/UECC-* directory
(WINEDEBUG=+setupapi shows the FIXME line instead of the crash).

--- a/dlls/cfgmgr32/main.c	2026-09-29 13:46:46
+++ b/dlls/cfgmgr32/main.c	2026-09-29 13:46:46
@@ -199,8 +199,17 @@
         notify_filter.handle.dbch_handle = filter->u.DeviceHandle.hTarget;
         break;
     case CM_NOTIFY_FILTER_TYPE_DEVICEINSTANCE:
-        FIXME( "CM_NOTIFY_FILTER_TYPE_DEVICEINSTANCE is not supported!\n" );
-        return CR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED;
+        /* SILO PATCH: not implemented, but hand back a real, inert context instead of an error. Steam's
+         * steamclient64 ignores this return value and later passes whatever is in *notify_handle to
+         * CM_Unregister_Notification — which crashed TEKKEN 8 on every exit. A context with no
+         * registration never fires, and unregistering it is safe (I_ScUnregisterDeviceNotification(NULL)
+         * returns FALSE without touching anything). */
+        FIXME( "CM_NOTIFY_FILTER_TYPE_DEVICEINSTANCE is not supported, returning an inert notification\n" );
+        if (!(ctx = calloc( 1, sizeof(*ctx) ))) return CR_OUT_OF_MEMORY;
+        ctx->user_data = user_data;
+        ctx->callback = callback;
+        *notify_handle = ctx;
+        return CR_SUCCESS;
     default:
         return CR_INVALID_DATA;
     }
@@ -232,6 +241,8 @@
     TRACE( "(%s %p %p %p)\n", debugstr_CM_NOTIFY_FILTER( filter ), context, callback, notify_context );
 
     if (!notify_context) return CR_FAILURE;
+    /* SILO PATCH: never leave the caller's handle uninitialised on a failure path. */
+    *notify_context = NULL;
     if (!filter || !callback || filter->cbSize != sizeof(*filter)) return CR_INVALID_DATA;
 
     return create_notify_context( filter, notify_context, callback, context );
